 Here is an open-ended response based on my experience shopping at a weekly farmers' market:

As someone who enjoys plain and fresh produce, I tend to be more interested in size-conscious buyers rather than high-end eating contests. Despite this, I'm always made happy when perusing the rows of tomatoes being harvested or fresh broccoli being chopped into florets.

I often pass by stalls offering both local and seasonal produce. It's rare that I have extra time for long restocking checkouts but when it is, it's filled with many varieties of fruits and vegetables to choose from. The oranges here are ripe as desired and very easy to handle;
